 'solar-system':[['A system held by gravity','The solar system includes small bodies as well as planets. Classifications describe shared features; distance alone does not make an object a planet.'],['Challenge the model','Our explorer compresses size, distance and time. Identify one wrong conclusion a viewer might draw if they assumed it was to scale.']],
 mars:[['Evidence and habitability','Minerals and landforms can provide evidence of past water. Water is relevant to habitability, but its presence does not establish that life existed.'],['Design with constraints','Choose one limitation for a Mars settlement: radiation, water, energy or communication delay. What would you need to know before evaluating a solution?']],
 sun:[['Different stages of a journey','The roughly eight-minute light journey is from the solar surface to Earth. Energy transport inside the Sun involves very different processes and timescales.'],['Explain a pattern','How can Earth’s rotation explain day and night without requiring the Sun to orbit Earth? Use a diagram with clear labels.']],
 elephants:[['Structure and function','A muscular hydrostat changes shape through coordinated muscle action. A flexible structure can provide both strength and fine control, with different trade-offs from a rigid arm.'],['Look at the ecosystem','Consider an elephant’s effects on vegetation, seed dispersal and water access. Could the same activity benefit some organisms and challenge others?']],
 rhinos:[['Adaptation in context','A browsing mouth is useful for selecting leaves and shoots. Physical traits should be understood in relation to behaviour, habitat and evolutionary history.'],['Compare evidence','What observations would help distinguish browsing from grazing? Avoid inferring an animal’s complete diet from one photograph.']],
 'rift-valley':[['A long geological process','Continental extension can form fault-bounded basins and influence volcanism. A visible crack is not the entire rifting process or a precise timetable for a future ocean.'],['Reason across timescales','Why can small annual movements create large landforms over millions of years? Explain why a short video cannot show the process at real speed.']],
 'water-cycle':[['Many pathways and stores','Water moves among atmosphere, surface water, ice, living organisms and groundwater. Residence times differ. A circular diagram simplifies a network of possible paths.'],['Challenge a simple diagram','Where would groundwater, transpiration and long-term ice storage fit? Explain why the cycle has no single compulsory starting point.']],
 algorithms:[['Correctness before confidence','An algorithm should have a clear goal and defined inputs. Test ordinary cases and boundary cases instead of assuming one successful run proves correctness.'],['Compare two solutions','Can two correct routes differ in number of steps or clarity? Choose a criterion before claiming that one is better.']],
 ai:[['Generated language is not verification','A fluent response can contain unsupported claims. Grounding, evaluation and human judgement address different problems; no one measure guarantees correctness.'],['Check a claim','Select a harmless claim from a digital tool. Find an independent reliable source and describe whether it supports the exact claim, a weaker version or neither.']],
